         test statistic for large sample sizes.
     correction : bool, optional
         If True, then a continuity correction is used for the chisquare
-        distribution (if exact is False.)
+        distribution (if exact is False.) As in R's ``mcnemar.test``, the
+        correction of 1 is applied only if ``|n1 - n2| >= 1``, where n1 and
+        n2 are the off-diagonal counts. Otherwise the statistic is not
+        corrected.
+
+        .. versionchanged:: 0.15.1
+
+           The correction is no longer applied if ``|n1 - n2|`` is smaller
+           than 1. Previously it was always subtracted, so that tables with
+           equal off-diagonal counts had a positive statistic and a p-value
+           below 1. If both off-diagonal counts are zero, the chisquare
+           statistic and p-value are now nan instead of inf and 0 when the
+           correction is used.
 
